From ddf8977a74706579e4516acfc6809479e860d3d7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 02:42:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] IR: SSA promotion and SCCP, dead code and CFG cleanup take
 vectors (#141)

A function with vectors stayed unpromoted, so Tier 1 refused it at
promotion. Now promotion and SCCP, dead code and CFG cleanup take it,
as they take a function whose only SIMD values are masks (#179):

- a slot of a vector type, read and written whole at its type, promotes
  as a scalar's does;
- both rewrites size and copy the vector constants' payloads, which
  each IR_VCONST indexes as before;
- SCCP never takes a vector for a constant (ir_optimize_transfer). A
  v4i32 addition isn't an i128 one, a constant bitcast to a vector
  would fold so, and IR_CONST has no vector type.

GVN, LICM, SROA and the inliner still refuse every SIMD function, and
Tier 1's selection still refuses vectors, which now meet it there.

test-ir-simd runs a function of each vector width through a vector
slot, an addition, two compares and a selection, as lowered, promoted
and optimized by both paths, on the shared interpreter: each returns the
mask its lanes give. Its boundary fixture now expects promotion and
SCCP/DCE/CFG to take a vector constant's result. test-ir-source --simd
counts the vector functions that promote, and test-tier1-cfg-source
--simd allocates them promoted, as any other.

